noma  Lump is benign on imaging and  consistent with fibrocystic changes on clinical exam     Physical Exam  The left breast showed a 1 2cm non tender  well defined  ovoid   rubbery and mobile mass at 4 o clock  2cm from the areola     Ultrasound was used to evaluate the lesion and showed a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  lesion that was  ill defined  ovoid  solid and cystic and heterogeneously  hypoechoic and isoechoic     Assessment  Based on the clinical history and physical examination  an FNAB is  warranted     Procedure  The procedure and potential complications were explained to the  patient  who understood the purpose  risks  and benefits of the procedure  The  patient confirmed name  date of birth  laterality  and lesion to be aspirated   Written consent was obtained     The biopsy procedure was performed by palpation     Three aspirates were performed using 25 gauge needles with local anesthesia and  without complications   4 slides were stained for immediate evaluation  Additional tissue was submitted  for further evaluation     The procedure was performed by Darcy Kerr  Fellow     Disposition  The immediate interpretation findings were discussed with the  patient  Erin Sullivan MD was notified of the preliminary results by personal  communication at 5 00 p m           The signing pathologist attests that he she performed the procedure or  if  performed by a resident or fellow  directed and supervised the FNA procedure and  was immediately available to further assist the resident fellow before  during  and after the procedure  and has reviewed and confirmed the interpretation of  slides stained for immediate evaluation            Electronically Signed Out By  Ivan A Chebib MD on REMOVED_DATE 10 14       CLINICAL HISTORY  Left breast lump for 1 month         SPECIMEN SOURCE  A  BREAST FNA BIOPSY  LEFT    GROSS DESCRIPTION  A  BREAST FNA BIOPSY  LEFT  Received 3 slides in ETOH  Received 3 air dried  slides           Specimen  BREAST FNA BIOPSY  LEFT       report_end  , Positive.
