Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final  Type  Surgical Pathology  Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Massachusetts General Hospital  Boston  MA  REMOVED_CASE_ID  Tel  617  REMOVED_DATE    Molecular Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  FISH Analysis      Accession     REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME   DOB  REMOVED_DATE  Age  57   Sex  F  MRN   REMOVED_CASE_ID   Institution  MGH  Location  YAW 9  BREAST ONC  Date of Collection  REMOVED_DATE  Date of Accession  REMOVED_DATE  Reported  REMOVED_DATE 13 32  Results To   Michaela J Higgins MB BCh      CLINICAL HISTORY   Breast Carcinoma    SPECIMENS RECEIVED   A  Molecular test for  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID     GROSS DESCRIPTION   Block from Newton Wellesley Hospital      SLIDE BLOCK DESCRIPTION    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   REMOVED_CASE_ID               TEST PERFORMED    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  FISH ANALYSIS    INDICATION FOR TEST Breast Carcinoma    Outside surgical consult case  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   REMOVED_CASE_ID   Newton Wellesley Hospital  Newton  MA    RESULTS    Fibroblast Growth Factor Receptor   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   gene amplification    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Reference Probe Copy Number Ratio  REMOVED_DATE    INTERPRETATION   The FISH data are consistent with NO amplification of the  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  gene     TEST INFORMATION   Aberrations involving the fibroblast growth factor receptor 1   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   gene have  been noted in tumors of multiple types  including certain lung  breast  ovarian   skeletal muscle  melanocytic and hematopoietic neoplasms   1  Amplification of  the  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  gene was recently identified as a significant and common finding  22   by FISH  in a cohort of squamous cell carcinomas of the lung   2     The assay performed on this patient uses fluorescence in situ hybridization   FISH  on formalin fixed paraffin embedded tumor specimens to analyze  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  gene  amplification status  Briefly  5 micron sections of formalin fixed  paraffin embedded tumor material were prepared and an H E section reviewed to  select regions for hybridization that contain a majority of tumor cells  A  dual color FISH assay was performed using Bacterial Artificial Chromosome probe  CTD  REMOVED_CASE_ID  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   chromosome 8p   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  locus  home brew  and a copy number control   centromere 8  Abbott Vysis 06 REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  or 06 REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID       Signal quantitation was used to generate a  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  centromere 8 ratio   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  to  Centromere 8 ratios are interpreted as follows  REMOVED_DATE to REMOVED_DATE is considered  borderline for amplification  REMOVED_DATE to REMOVED_DATE is considered low level amplification   and greater than REMOVED_DATE or clustered  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  signals that are too numerous to count  would be considered highly amplified  CPT codes for this assay are  REMOVED_CASE_ID  x 2     References  1  Turner N and Grose R  Fibroblast growth factor signaling  from  development to cancer  Nature Reviews Cancer 10 116   REMOVED_CASE_ID     2  Weiss J  Sos  M  et al  Frequent and focal  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  amplification associates  with therapeutically tractable  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  dependency in squamous cell lung cancer   Sci Transl Med 2 62  62ra93   REMOVED_CASE_ID       This test was developed  and its performance characteristics were determined by  the MGH Diagnostic Molecular Pathology Laboratory  It has not been cleared or  approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  The FDA has determined that  such clearance or approval is not necessary  This test is used for clinical  purposes  Pursuant to the requirements of CLIA  88  this laboratory has  established and verified the test s accuracy and precision     Questions concerning these values should be addressed to Dr  A  John Iafrate at   617  REMOVED_DATE MGH internal address  Diagnostic Molecular Pathology Laboratory   Massachusetts General Hospital  55 Fruit St   Warren 508  Boston  MA  REMOVED_CASE_ID             Electronically Signed Out By  Anthony John Iafrate MD         PART   Molecular test for  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID        report_end  , Negative.
