Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 07  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 07  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  Same Day Surgery Unit Path Subspecialty Service  Breast 1 Results To  MICHELE ANNETTE GADD  M D  Resident  James E  Davis  M D  Consulting Pathologist s   Andrew E Rosenberg  MD Signed Out by  Kristina Braaten  M D  CLINICAL DATA  Atypical vascular lesion  FINAL DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISION  HEMANGIOMA WITH ATYPICAL FEATURES  REMOVED_DATE CM  SEE NOTE   HEALING BIOPSY SITE  NOTE  The lesion shows limited atypical morphologic features in the form of mild cytologic atypia and foci of architectural complexity  However  the lesion is fairly well demarcated  i e   the vascular spaces do not dissect through fat in an infiltrating manner  In addition  there is an overall lobulated architecture  and the vascular spaces are well formed and invested by fibrous stroma  For these reasons  we feel the lesion is benign and does not represent angiosarcoma  The lesion is focally present a fraction of a millimeter from the margin  By his her signature below  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm portion of unoriented breast tissue with a localization wire in place  Also connected to the localization wire is a separate piece of fibrofatty tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm  both portions of fibrofatty tissue are inked black  Sectioning of both the larger and smaller portions of fibrofatty tissue reveals no mass lesions or other gross abnormalities  The larger of fibrofatty tissue  measuring 2 5cm in maximal dimension  is submitted in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   with  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  containing the tissue adjacent to the localization wire  The smaller fragment of fibrofatty tissue is bivalved  revealing no abnormalities and is submitted in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Final Diagnosis by Kristina Braaten M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART   BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISION  report_end  , Negative.
